{"reference":"Psalms 121","book":"Psalms","chapter":121,"status":"pending","sections":[{"kind":"surrounding_passages","title":"Nearby Psalms","blocks":[{"id":"block_1","text":"Psalm 121 stands among Psalms 120–134, a group that includes Songs of Ascents oriented toward worship. In the wider Book V, communal psalms also preserve memories of sanctuary destruction and Babylonian exile alongside thanksgiving for return, festival praise, and meditation on Torah. This setting is disputed, but it can help readers hear Psalm 121 as part of a larger collection concerned with communal worship and remembrance.","verse_refs":["Psalms 120:1-7","Psalms 122:1-9","Psalms 123:1-4","Psalms 124:1-8","Psalms 125:1-5","Psalms 126:1-6","Psalms 127:1-5","Psalms 128:1-6","Psalms 129:1-8","Psalms 130:1-8","Psalms 131:1-3","Psalms 132:1-18","Psalms 133:1-3","Psalms 134:1-3"],"provenance_refs":["reader_path_psalms_121_33c2646838fb8c688c05f364"],"confidence":"high","interpretation_level":"disputed"}]}],"generated_metadata":null}